Here's a stupid way to die...
sysong the Archaeologist is cruising through the dungeon when he finds an
old bones pile. Its contents (this is too painful) were: 
(cursed) gauntlets of power, a +3 dwarvish mithril-coat, and
a +2 cloak of protection.
Wow I think, what a great stash. How could any one die with such great stuff?
(Little did I know, I was about to find out....)
I also find four of five rings: they were unidentified. Having no 
identify scrolls and having already put on the cursed gauntlets 
(I had an ScrolloRC), I think: So!
I'll just use that tip that I picked up on this newsgroup and drop the rings
down a sink.
The first one goes plop and it's a ring of searching. So I get it back.
The second one goes glump and it's a ring of teleport control.
The third one goes... (and you get the point.)
Anyway, I think: Wouldn't it be neat if I can drink from the sink and get 
those rings back? (Happens othertimes with sinks I encounter for the first
time. There are rings in the sink.) So I take off my coat and cloak (don't
want them destroyed when I turn into a Grey Dragon) and drink. Lo and behold,
the sink has toxic wastes and I become......
	a yellow light.
Disappointed, but not daunted, I confront the situation. I am stressed, 
so I drop all my stuff (except Excalibur) by the sink. 
And then, what should happen but a rock troll should come by and start 
hacking away at me.
Well, my archaeologist maintained its ground and killed the rock troll. Only
thing was, I lost a lot of hit points in the bargain and a jello cube creeps
into the room. Now I don't want to run away lest the rock troll revives 
and uses my goodies or (gasp!) the jello cube eats all my goodies. So I 
pick up all my equipment when --BAM-- the thing paralyzes me.
And then, Mr. rock troll revives and finishes his job.
sigh...
Oh well, my questions are as follows:
1) Is there any way to avoid the paralysis of a gelatinous cube? (like a
paralysis resistance intrinsic? I had sleep restistance BTW)
2) Would I have been able to recover those rings from the sink?
(and if so, will they be waiting for me on the bones level? [RoTC is very 
useful])
Somewhat unrelated:
Someone told me once that by eating a troll corpse, you regenerate your
hit points faster. I think there is no regeneration intrinsic, but could
I be wrong?
-sysong



